<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38233" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prĕcātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		precor. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a praying</i>, <i>prayer</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sollemnis comitiorum precatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Mur. 1, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">precatione uti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tusc. 1, 47, 114</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">precationem facere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					39, 18</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 28, 2, 3, § 10</span></i>:
			auguralis, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 351</span></i>
			Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, concr., <i>a form of
				prayer</i> with superstitious people (post-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Plin. 28, 4,
				9, § 42</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
